From 74d1875c2995706fb6cef2fa26ab55ee0b0a04d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: root <root@srv1843077.hstgr.cloud>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 16:11:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] hud: declare spectator and POV requirements, and surface
 them in the editor

An element that will not draw was previously indistinguishable from one placed
badly, because nothing in the engine declared why. hud.h had no spectator flag
at all: the behaviour lived as `cl.spectator == cl.autocam` inside 15 draw
functions, so it could not be queried by the built-in editor either.

Two flags, because the engine has two distinct behaviours and conflating them
would mislabel 32 elements:

- HUD_SPEC_REQUIRED: only meaningful while spectating. Just `tracking`.
- HUD_NEEDS_POV: needs a player POV. Draws fine while playing and while
  spectating a tracked player; hidden only when free-flying. Covers the
  inventory and status set (health, armor, ammo, guns, items, powerups, keys,
  sigils).

CAM_NONE is 0 and CAM_TRACK is 1, which is why `cl.spectator == cl.autocam`
holds in both the playing and the tracking case; reading it as "spectator only"
would have been wrong for every element except tracking.

/state now reports both as named booleans rather than making clients decode a
bitfield they would have to keep in sync with hud.h by hand, plus the engine's
viewing context (spectator, tracking, demoplayback).

The editor gains a Spectator filter toggle, per-row badges, and replaces the
generic "no position" notice with the actual reason: hidden, spectator-only, or
free-flying without a POV.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FqUfMu4JRqFSaazvAD6kyH
