Subject: [PATCH 3/6] hud_web: report whether a proportional font is actually
 loaded

A HUD editor that shows every element's `proportional` cvar as an editable
field implies those fields do something. Usually they do not.

font_facepath defaults to empty, which makes FontClear zero the face, so
FontFixedWidth takes its `max_length * 8 * scale` branch and `proportional 1`
is inert on every element. That is the default state of a stock install.

Worse, a client cannot detect this: Draw_InitFont discards FontCreate's return
value, so a saved config naming a font that no longer resolves leaves
font_facepath set, no face loaded, and nothing reported anywhere. Non-empty
facepath does not imply a usable face.

Adds FontProportionalLoaded() (false by definition without FreeType, where
FontFixedWidth is already a macro) and reports it in /state alongside the
active facepath and console charset. The editor marks affected parameters
inert and says why, rather than presenting a dead control as live. Values stay
editable and still save, because they become meaningful the moment a face
loads.

Found by studying hud_common.c's SCR_HUD_DrawNum2 against fonts.c rather than
assuming the rendering path; the same study shows `proportional` is also
ignored by the picture-drawing styles, which the field's tooltip now notes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FqUfMu4JRqFSaazvAD6kyH
---
 src/fonts.c | 5 +++++
 src/fonts.h | 6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/fonts.c b/src/fonts.c
index 3cb7e874..aaea9ea1 100644
--- a/src/fonts.c
+++ b/src/fonts.c
@@ -396,6 +396,11 @@ static qbool FontCreate(int grouping, const char* userpath)
 
 // Used for allocating space - if we just measure the string then other hud elements
 //   might move around as content changes, which is probably not what is wanted
+qbool FontProportionalLoaded(void)
+{
+	return R_TextureReferenceIsValid(proportional_fonts[0].master);
+}
+
 int FontFixedWidth(int max_length, float scale, qbool digits_only, qbool proportional)
 {
 	if (!proportional || !R_TextureReferenceIsValid(proportional_fonts[0].master)) {
diff --git a/src/fonts.h b/src/fonts.h
index ed88668a..83dbe3c8 100644
--- a/src/fonts.h
+++ b/src/fonts.h
@@ -5,8 +5,14 @@
 #ifdef EZ_FREETYPE_SUPPORT
 void FontInitialise(void);
 int FontFixedWidth(int max_length, float scale, qbool digits_only, qbool proportional);
+// Whether a proportional face is actually usable right now. font_facepath being
+// non-empty does NOT imply this: Draw_InitFont discards FontCreate's result, so a
+// config naming a font that no longer resolves leaves the cvar set with no face
+// loaded, and every `proportional 1` silently renders at 8px instead.
+qbool FontProportionalLoaded(void);
 #else
 #define FontFixedWidth(max_length, scale, digits_only, proportional) (max_length * 8.0f * scale)
+#define FontProportionalLoaded() (false)
 #endif
 
 qbool FontAlterCharCoordsWide(float* x, float* y, wchar ch, qbool bigchar, float scale, qbool proportional);
